ctk (2026.09.02-1+neuro3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the DGraph build-time helper as usr/libexec/ctk/DGraph in libctk-dev
    and export CTK_DGRAPH_EXECUTABLE from the installed CTKConfig.cmake.
    ctkMacroSetupPlugins runs it at configure time, and upstream only ever
    builds it into CTK's own build tree with no install rule, so every
    consumer of the plugin framework (MITK's BlueBerry) failed with
    "Executable doesn't exist!" against installed CTK.

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:23:02 -0700

ctk (2026.09.02-1+neuro2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix find_package(CTK) for consumers. CTK_INSTALL_CMAKE_DIR and
    CTK_INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR were passed as absolute paths, so CTKConfig.cmake
    computed include directories as "${PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR}//usr/include/ctk",
    and libctk-dev.install re-homed usr/lib/CMake/ctk into
    usr/lib/<triplet>/cmake/ctk, nesting it one level deeper as
    .../cmake/ctk/ctk/ where CMake does not look. find_package(CTK REQUIRED)
    therefore failed outright on a system with libctk-dev installed. Pass both
    directories relative to the prefix and install the cmake directory where it
    is generated.

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:12:01 -0700

ctk (2026.09.02-1+neuro1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable the CTK plugin framework and widgets
    (-DCTK_ENABLE_PluginFramework=ON, -DCTK_ENABLE_Widgets=ON). The current
    build ships only libCTKCore and libCTKDICOMCore, but libCTKPluginFramework
    is what MITK's BlueBerry application framework and every org.mitk.* plugin
    are built on, and CTKWidgets is required alongside it. 3D Slicer needs the
    same components. Upstream Fedora packaging enables these plus VTK, ITK and
    PythonQt wrapping; only the two needed here are turned on, to avoid new
    dependencies (PythonQt and QtTesting are not in Debian).

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:53:39 -0700

